  "notes": "Godan verb ({五段動詞|ごだんどうし}), ぐ-ending.\n- Negative: {引|ひ}き{継|つ}がない\n- Polite: {引|ひ}き{継|つ}ぎます\n- Te-form: {引|ひ}き{継|つ}いで\n- Past: {引|ひ}き{継|つ}いだ\n- Noun form: {引|ひ}き{継|つ}ぎ (handover)\n\nUSAGE:\nVery common in business contexts for job handovers and transitions. The noun form {引|ひ}き{継|つ}ぎ is equally common and refers to the handover process itself. Also used for inheriting traditions, customs, or family businesses.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {業務|ぎょうむ}を{引|ひ}き{継|つ}ぐ: to take over duties\n- {伝統|でんとう}を{引|ひ}き{継|つ}ぐ: to inherit a tradition\n- {引|ひ}き{継|つ}ぎ{書|しょ}: handover document\n- {引|ひ}き{継|つ}ぎ{期間|きかん}: handover period",
